[Rendered](https://github.com/conradludgate/rfcs/blob/postfix-match/text/0000-postfix-match.md)

An alternative postfix syntax for match expressions that allows for interspersing match statements with function chains

```rust
foo.bar().baz.match {
    _ => {}
}
```

as syntax sugar for

```rust
match foo.bar().baz {
    _ => {}
}
```

[Rendered](https://github.com/Jules-Bertholet/rfcs/blob/static_in_pattern/text/3305-static-in-pattern.md)

Proposes allowing patterns to refer to statics, including trusted extern statics.

```rust
static NUMBER: i32 = 42;

fn foo(scrutinee: i32) {
    match scrutinee {
        NUMBER => println!("yes"),
        _ => println!("no"),
    }
}
```

[Internals thread](https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/allow-non-mut-statics-in-patterns/17145)
[Full implementation](https://github.com/Jules-Bertholet/rust/tree/statics_in_patterns)

[Rendered](https://github.com/knickish/rfcs/blob/3341/text/3342-anonymous_associated_types.md)

Create new anonymous types in trait impl blocks to use as associated types. Short example: 
```rust
pub trait MyTrait{
    type Fields;
}

pub struct MyStruct{
    field1: usize
}

impl MyTrait for MyStruct{
    type Fields = enum { Field1(usize) };
}
```
